      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "A fundamental new class of quantum matter, with experimentally decisive transport phenomena and broad influence on condensed-matter physics.",
        "attribution": "Kane and Mele supplied the defining quantum-spin-Hall theory, while Molenkamp provided a landmark experimental realization.",
        "maturity": "The phenomena and their theoretical framework have been repeatedly confirmed and remain central to topological materials research.",
        "uncertainties": [
