        "Harald Rose",
        "Knut Urban",
        "Maximilian Haider"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Aberration correction transformed electron microscopy into a quantitatively powerful sub-angstrom probe of matter.",
        "attribution": "Rose developed essential correction concepts, and Urban and Haider were central to their practical realization and scientific demonstration.",
        "maturity": "Its impact is longstanding, reproducible across instruments, and visible throughout modern materials science.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The division of credit among the wider community that developed corrected electron optics must be examined."
        ]
      }
    },
