        "Michele Parrinello",
        "Roberto Car"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The method made predictive first-principles simulations of atomic motion broadly practical and altered the study of condensed matter, chemistry, and materials.",
        "attribution": "Car and Parrinello are the clearly identifiable originators of the named method.",
        "maturity": "The approach has endured for decades, generated a large methodological lineage, and is strongly connected to experimentally testable materials physics.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Its interdisciplinary character raises a question of whether its principal recognition should fall under physics or chemistry."
        ]
      }
    },
